Lab 5: Implementing a Single-Site IdM Topology
Objectives
By the end of this lab, students will be able to:

Understand the architecture and components of a single-site Identity Management (IdM) topology
Install and configure a primary IdM server with integrated DNS
Deploy and configure IdM replica servers for redundancy
Configure network settings and DNS resolution for IdM infrastructure
Test replication functionality between IdM servers
Verify high availability and failover capabilities
Troubleshoot common IdM topology issues
Prerequisites
Before starting this lab, students should have:

Basic understanding of Linux system administration
Familiarity with DNS concepts and configuration
Knowledge of LDAP directory services fundamentals
Experience with command-line interface operations
Understanding of network configuration basics
Familiarity with systemd service management
Required Knowledge Areas
Linux file permissions and ownership
Basic networking concepts (IP addressing, DNS)
Understanding of Kerberos authentication principles
Familiarity with certificate management concepts
