Task 1: Prepare the Environment and Install Primary IdM Server
Subtask 1.1: Configure System Prerequisites
First, we'll prepare all three servers with the necessary system configurations.

Step 1: Update all systems

Execute on all three servers:

# Update system packages
sudo dnf update -y

# Install essential tools
sudo dnf install -y vim wget curl net-tools bind-utils
Step 2: Configure hostnames and hosts file

On the primary server (192.168.1.10):

# Set hostname
sudo hostnamectl set-hostname idm-primary.lab.local

# Configure /etc/hosts
sudo tee /etc/hosts << EOF
127.0.0.1   localhost localhost.localdomain
192.168.1.10    idm-primary.lab.local idm-primary
192.168.1.11    idm-replica1.lab.local idm-replica1
192.168.1.12    idm-replica2.lab.local idm-replica2
EOF
On the first replica server (192.168.1.11):

# Set hostname
sudo hostnamectl set-hostname idm-replica1.lab.local

# Configure /etc/hosts (same content as above)
sudo tee /etc/hosts << EOF
127.0.0.1   localhost localhost.localdomain
192.168.1.10    idm-primary.lab.local idm-primary
192.168.1.11    idm-replica1.lab.local idm-replica1
192.168.1.12    idm-replica2.lab.local idm-replica2
EOF
On the second replica server (192.168.1.12):

# Set hostname
sudo hostnamectl set-hostname idm-replica2.lab.local

# Configure /etc/hosts (same content as above)
sudo tee /etc/hosts << EOF
127.0.0.1   localhost localhost.localdomain
192.168.1.10    idm-primary.lab.local idm-primary
192.168.1.11    idm-replica1.lab.local idm-replica1
192.168.1.12    idm-replica2.lab.local idm-replica2
