Subtask 1.2: Install IdM Server Packages
Step 1: Install IdM server packages on primary server

Execute on the primary server only:

# Install IdM server with integrated DNS
sudo dnf module enable idm:DL1/server -y
sudo dnf install -y ipa-server ipa-server-dns

# Verify installation
rpm -qa | grep ipa-server
Subtask 1.3: Configure Primary IdM Server
Step 1: Run IdM server installation

Execute on the primary server:

# Install and configure IdM server with integrated DNS
sudo ipa-server-install \
    --realm=LAB.LOCAL \
    --domain=lab.local \
    --ds-password=RedHat123! \
    --admin-password=RedHat123! \
    --hostname=idm-primary.lab.local \
    --setup-dns \
    --forwarder=8.8.8.8 \
    --forwarder=8.8.4.4 \
    --reverse-zone=1.168.192.in-addr.arpa. \
    --unattended
Important Notes:

The installation process takes 10-15 minutes
Use strong passwords in production environments
The --unattended flag prevents interactive prompts
Step 2: Verify IdM server installation

# Check IdM services status
sudo systemctl status ipa

# Verify Kerberos authentication
kinit admin
# Enter password: RedHat123!

# List Kerberos ticket
klist

# Test IdM command-line tools
ipa user-find admin
Step 3: Configure DNS resolution

# Update /etc/resolv.conf to use local DNS
sudo tee /etc/resolv.conf << EOF
search lab.local
nameserver 192.168.1.10
nameserver 8.8.8.8
EOF

# Test DNS resolution
nslookup idm-primary.lab.local
dig @192.168.1.10 lab.local SOA
Task 2: Set Up DNS and Network Configurations
Subtask 2.1: Configure DNS Zones and Records
Step 1: Create additional DNS records

